From: AGaMEMnon contributors
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] target/riscv: fix nested ADIv5 config lookup

Gerrit 9590 stores the ADIv5 configuration as `adi_pc` inside
`riscv_private_config`.  riscv_examine() must pass that member to
adiv5_verify_config(), not reinterpret the start of the enclosing object.
The latter reads the enabled ebreak booleans as a pointer, rejects the DAP
configuration, and falls through to a JTAG scan on an SWD transport.

diff --git a/src/target/riscv/riscv.c b/src/target/riscv/riscv.c
index cfe1c2ee1..30fa2264b 100644
--- a/src/target/riscv/riscv.c
+++ b/src/target/riscv/riscv.c
@@ -2482,7 +2482,8 @@ static int riscv_examine(struct target *target)
 	RISCV_INFO(info);
 	uint32_t dtm_version;
 
-	struct adiv5_private_config *pc = target->private_config;
+	struct riscv_private_config *config = target->private_config;
+	struct adiv5_private_config *pc = &config->adi_pc;
 	if (adiv5_verify_config(pc) == ERROR_OK) {
 		dtm_version = 1;
 		info->alternative_dmi = true;
-- 
